 has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/herculaneum"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/herculaneum.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Herculaneum</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Herculaneum was an ancient Roman town on the Bay of Naples, at modern Ercolano, buried by the eruption of Mount Vesuvius in 79 CE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/hercules-kassel"><span class="enc-name">Hercules (Kassel)</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Hercules in Kassel is a monumental statue of Hercules standing on an octagonal pyramid and castle-like structure at the top of the Bergpark Wilhelmshöhe.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/hercynian-forest"><span class="enc-name">Hercynian Forest</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Hercynian Forest was the name given by Greek and Roman writers to the great forest of central Europe, stretching east from the Rhine across southern Germany to the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/hereford"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hereford.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Hereford</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Hereford is a cathedral city on the River Wye in western England, the county town of Herefordshire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/herero-and-nama-genocide"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/herero-and-nama-genocide.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Herero and Nama genocide</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The Herero and Nama genocide was the extermination of the Herero and Nama peoples in German South West Africa (now Namibia) by the German Empire between 1904 and 1908.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/herero-people"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/herero-people.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Herero people</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Herero are a Bantu-speaking, cattle-herding people of central and northern Namibia and neighbouring Botswana.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/herero-wars"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/herero-wars.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Herero Wars</span><span class="enc-type">War · 1904–1908</span><span class="enc-snip">The Herero Wars were the colonial wars in German South West Africa, now Namibia, in which the Herero and then the Nama rose against German rule in 1904.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/herford"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/herford.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Herford</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Herford is a town in eastern Westphalia, in the German state of North Rhine-Westphalia, north-east of Bielefeld.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/herge"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/herge.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Hergé</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Hergé was the pen name of Georges Remi, a Belgian cartoonist best known for &quot;The Adventures of Tintin&quot;, which began in 1929.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/herihor"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/herihor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Herihor</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Herihor was an Egyptian army officer who became High Priest of Amun at Thebes around 1080 BCE, in the last years of Ramesses XI and the Twentieth Dynasty.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/herisau"><span class="enc-name">Herisau</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Herisau is a town in north-eastern Switzerland and the capital of the half-canton of Appenzell Ausserrhoden.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/herius-asinius"><span class="enc-name">Herius Asinius</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Herius Asinius was a commander of the Marrucini, an Italic people of the Adriatic coast, during the Social War against Rome.</span></a></li></ul>
